    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d155-a16">

                <pb facs="0363" n="339" sameAs="frus:frus1902app1/pg339"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Olney to Mr. de Kotzebue.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 53.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1896-05-01"><hi rendition="#italic">May 1,
                        1896</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your note of the 10th ultimo,
                    in regard to the complaint of Captain Dahlberg, of the Russian bark <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hans</hi>, I have the honor to say that the Department
                    of Justice has appointed an examiner to collect the evidence necessary to
                    ascertain whether Captain Dahlberg was unlawfully imprisoned, and whether his
                    rights growing out of the treaty between the United States and Russia were
                    violated.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Richard Olney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
